Subject: [PATCH] Shell: Get games, games downloaded from your own server
 instead of embedded

Get games (Shell/ShellStore.swift) lists the server's shell catalogue (scripts/publish_shell.py), downloads a game's framework into the
app's own Frameworks folder and its romfs.img into Documents/games/<title ID>/ with the per-game app's resumable, checked download
(GameDataSyncCore.swift). In LiveContainer the app's bundle is writable; iOS runs the new framework once LiveContainer's Force Sign has
signed it, which the screen reads from the framework's code signature. build_shell.sh DM_SHELL_EMBED=0 builds the app with no game in it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: games for the one-app shell downloaded from a self-hosted server, signed by LiveContainer's Force Sign
Issue: none (the fork Valtterios/NX2Apple has no issue tracker; branch duo-upstream)

